  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following statement(s) is (are) correct about the spectrum of hydrogen atom?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The ratio of the longest wavelength to the shortest wavelength in Balmer series is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "There is an overlap between the wavelength ranges of Balmer and Paschen series.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The wavelengths of Lyman series are given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the shortest wavelength of Lyman series and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is an integer.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The wavelength ranges of Lyman and Balmer series do not overlap.",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A",
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0004_acbbc5f74209.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 189px;\" /></p><p>For Balmer Series:</p><p>Shortest wavelength,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Longest wavelength,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Range of energy level in Balmer series,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Range of energy level in Paschen&nbsp;series,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>144</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, no overlap.</p><p>For Lyman series:</p><p>For shortest wavelength,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>For general wavelength,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p><p>as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;should be an integer.</p><p>Range of energy level in Lyman series,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;Lyman and Balmer series wavelengths do not overlap.</p>"
  }
}